From: Holodor <noreply@holodor.local>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: qcom: add qcom,sm8750-ufshc compatible to ufs_qcom_of_match

sm8750.dtsi defines `compatible = "qcom,sm8750-ufshc", "qcom,ufshc", "jedec,ufs-2.0"`,
but `ufs_qcom_of_match[]` only matched `qcom,sm8550-ufshc` and `qcom,sm8650-ufshc`
to `ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata` (`.no_phy_retention = true`). As a result, SM8750 fell
back to the generic `qcom,ufshc` entry with `spm_lvl = 3` (UFS_PM_LVL_3, link in
Hibern8 with PHY powered on) instead of `spm_lvl = 5` (UFS_PM_LVL_5, link off and
PHY powered down).

Leaving `ufs_mem_phy` (`1d80000.phy`) powered on across system suspend keeps
`RPMH_CXO_CLK` (`bi_tcxo`, which votes `xo.lvl = 0x3` in `SLEEP_TCS`) prepared and
leaves `vreg_l1j_0p91` (213 mA), `vreg_l3g_1p2` (18 mA), `vreg_l17b_2p5` (1300 mA),
and `vreg_bob2` enabled throughout `s2idle`, blocking AOSS/XO shutdown (`aosd`).

Map `qcom,sm8750-ufshc` to `ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata` like SM8550 and SM8650.
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -3005,6 +3005,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id ufs_qcom_of_match[] __maybe_unused = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,ufshc" },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8550-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8750-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sm8550_drvdata },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sa8255p-ufshc", .data = &ufs_qcom_sa8255p_drvdata },
 	{},
 };
